# Web3Forms access key. Get it from https://web3forms.com
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ is required: Web3Forms only accepts requests sent from the browser. It rejects
# server-side and proxied calls with "403 This method is not allowed" unless you have a paid
# plan and have safelisted your server IP.
#
# This value is inlined into the public JavaScript bundle. That is expected and safe here —
# Web3Forms states the access key is not a secret and works as an alias for your inbox.
# Spam is handled by the honeypot field plus Web3Forms' own filtering.
#
# Set it locally in .env.local, and on Vercel under Project > Settings > Environment Variables.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=your_actual_web3forms_access_key
